<p>
<font class="blocknum">1.</font><font class="step">&nbsp;&nbsp;Looking Up the User</p>
<p>Type in all or any portion of the users first name, last name, or their email, and then press the Lookup Profile button.
The user will be looked up in the corporate database and the ARA database. If the user does not exist as a user in the ARA database, their corporate information is pulled and the form is setup to create a new user in ARA. If the user exists in ARA, then the form is populated to update their information in ARA.<br><br>
<img src="images/hlp_users1.gif" alt="Populating the user information form"><br><br>
<p>
<font class="blocknum">2.</font><font class="step">&nbsp;&nbsp;Security and Job Title</p>
<p>Once a profile is created the user is able to access ARA. Once logged into ARA what users are allowed to see  and edit, as well as how they are involved in the ARA approval process are controlled by the Security Role and Job Title settings in the user record.</p>
<p>The user status defaults to active. It is recommended that if user access is terminated that the Inactive flag be set. This preserves the relationship the user may have had with any ARAs previously processed. In fact ARA will not allow you to delete users that have a pre-existing information associated with them.<br><br>
<img src="images/hlp_users2.gif" alt="Seeting the security role and job title in the user profile"><br><br>

<font class="blocknum">3.</font><font class="step">&nbsp;&nbsp;Editing a Profile</p>
<p>The bottom portion of the ARA Users page includes a list of all active users. The user's profile can be edited by clicking on the link with their user name. The display of users, the the sort that is applied, can be alternated by clicking on the column header. The column displaying the down arrow, is the current sort that has been applied.</p>
<img src="images/hlp_users3.gif" alt="List of users presented at bottom of page"><br><br>

<font class="blocknum">4.</font><font class="step">&nbsp;&nbsp;Deleting a Profile</p>
<p>Users can be deleted by clicking on the <i>trash-can</i> icon. Prior to deleting ARA will check to see if the user being deleted has any associated data. If they are associated with data in the system, deletion will not be allowed, and the user status will be set to inactive instead. Inactive users are not able to login into the system. Inactive users can be returned to their active status by updating their profile.</p>